<problem>
<!-- <title>Solve simple linear differential equations, general solutions</title> -->

<setup>


<function name="y" variables="t" symbolic="true">y</function>
<function name="ysol" variables="t" symbolic="true">C*e^(2t)</function>
<function name="x" variables="t" symbolic="true">x</function>
<function name="xsol" variables="t" symbolic="true">C*e^(-3t)</function>
<function name="m" variables="t" symbolic="true">m</function>
<function name="msol" variables="t" symbolic="true">C*e^(11t)</function>
<function name="v" variables="t" symbolic="true">v</function>
<function name="vsol" variables="t">C*e^t</function>

</setup>


If we aren't given the initial conditions, we cannot determine the exact solution of the differential equation.  For the following differential equations, give the general solution, which will be a function with an undetermined constant <m>C</m>.


<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<m>\displaystyle \frac{ dy }{ dt }=2$y</m>

<p><m>y(t)=</m> 
<answer>
<award symbolicEquality="true" simplifyOnCompare="true">$ysol </award>
</answer>
</p>
</exercise>


<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<m>x'(t)=-3$x (t) </m>

<p><m>x(t)=</m> 
<answer>
<award symbolicEquality="true" simplifyOnCompare="true">$xsol </award>
</answer>
</p>
</exercise>


<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<m>\displaystyle \frac{ dm }{ dt }=11$m (t)</m>.

<p><m>m(t)=</m> 
<answer>
<award symbolicEquality="true" simplifyOnCompare="true">$msol </award>
</answer>
</p>
</exercise>


<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<m>v'(t)=$v </m>.

<p><m>v(t)=</m> 
<answer>
<award symbolicEquality="true" simplifyOnCompare="true">$vsol </award>
</answer>
</p>

<hint>Recall, sometimes we write <m>y</m> to represent the function <em><m>$y (t)</m></em> as a shorthand notation.</hint>
</exercise>

  
<solution>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>
<m>y(t)=$ysol </m></p>
</exercise>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>
<m>x(t)=$xsol </m></p>
</exercise>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>
<m>m(t)=$msol </m></p>
</exercise>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>
<m>v(t)=$vsol </m></p>
</exercise>
</solution>


</problem>